@end quotation

@quotation
@strong{@anchor{Exercise 3.16}Exercise 3.16:} Ben Bitdiddle decides to write a
function to count the number of pairs in any list structure.  ``It's easy,''
he reasons.  ``The number of pairs in any structure is the number in the
@code{car} plus the number in the @code{cdr} plus one more to count the current
pair.''  So Ben writes the following function:

@example rust
fn count_pairs(x: &Value) -> u64 @{
    match x @{
        Value::Pair(cell) => @{
            count_pairs(&cell.car.borrow())
                + count_pairs(&cell.cdr.borrow())
                + 1
        @}
        _ => 0,
    @}
@}
@end example

